================================================================================
PARTS OF THIS REPOSITORY ARE GPL-2.0, AND HAVE TO BE
================================================================================

The MIT license above covers this project's own material: the documentation,
the shell and Python scripts under scripts/, and the collected data.

It does NOT cover the Linux kernel drivers. Those carry
`SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-2.0` in their own headers and stay GPL-2.0:

    build-6.12/gc5035.c        build-6.12/gc8034.c
    build-6.12/ipu-bridge.c    patches/**
    reference/**

This is not a preference, it is a condition inherited from the code they are
derived from. Their register tables are reproduced from existing GPL-2.0 work:

  * gc5035.c  — from the out-of-tree Alder Lake-M patch in intel/ipu6-drivers
                by liang.wang <liang1.wang@intel.com>, which derives from the
                ChromeOS series by Tomasz Figa <tfiga@chromium.org>.
                Copyright (c) 2020 Bitland Inc., 2020 Google LLC,
                2022 Intel Corporation.

  * gc8034.c  — from the Rockchip BSP.
                Copyright (C) 2017 Fuzhou Rockchip Electronics Co., Ltd.

GPL-2.0 requires derivative works to be distributed under the same terms. The
original copyright lines are preserved in the file headers, and the full chain
of provenance is documented in reference/README.md.

The drivers are meant for the mainline Linux kernel, where GPL-2.0 is required
anyway.


================================================================================
IN BREVE, IN ITALIANO
================================================================================

La licenza MIT qui sopra e' la piu' permissiva in uso reale: chiunque puo'
usare, copiare, modificare, distribuire e anche vendere questo lavoro, a una
sola condizione — mantenere la riga di copyright. Copre i documenti, gli
script e i dati raccolti.

I due driver del kernel restano GPL-2.0 e non e' una scelta: contengono
tabelle di registri prese da codice GPL-2.0 gia' esistente, e la GPL obbliga
chi le riusa a ridistribuirle alle stesse condizioni. E' la stessa licenza del
kernel Linux, dove quei driver sono destinati ad andare.

Nota: il nome nel copyright e' l'identificativo GitHub. Va sostituito con nome
e cognome veri quando si sciogliera' il reperto B1 di
docs/09-revisione-preinvio.md, che e' lo stesso nodo del `Signed-off-by`.
